WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.129
- I remember hearing about Greg 

00:00:04.129 --> 00:00:05.213
at ABCD Camp.

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:07.966
You know, people were comparing him to Bill Russell.

00:00:07.966 --> 00:00:09.426
I mean,

00:00:09.426 --> 00:00:13.304
you don't get compared to Bill Russell when you're 17 years old.

00:00:13.304 --> 00:00:15.932
- [Announcer]: Here's Oden backing in, doubled but he dunks.

00:00:16.766 --> 00:00:19.352
- Oden's having an outstanding ballgame.

00:00:20.228 --> 00:00:22.063
- We had our schools that we both liked.

00:00:22.063 --> 00:00:24.190
He liked Michigan State, I liked North Carolina.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:27.902
Our last visit that we took was together at Ohio State.

00:00:27.902 --> 00:00:31.406
We sat there in the arena talking to Thad Matta and

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.575
kinda looked at each other and was like,

00:00:34.242 --> 00:00:35.368
"Uh, are we gonna do this?"

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:39.289
- Me and Mike decided to come to the Ohio State University.

00:00:39.289 --> 00:00:40.248
- "You want to go to Ohio State?"

00:00:40.248 --> 00:00:41.750
He's like, "If it's cool with you."

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:42.959
You know, that's just how he is.

00:00:42.959 --> 00:00:44.419
- This was a place that we both

00:00:44.419 --> 00:00:46.004
felt comfortable being at,

00:00:46.004 --> 00:00:48.882
a place where we know we can grow as young men.

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:52.135
I wanted, you know, to bring a national championship here.

00:00:52.135 --> 00:00:53.928
- [Announcer]: Basket by Oden.

00:00:53.928 --> 00:00:55.889
- Our expectations going into the tournament, 

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:58.266
we felt like we were a championship-caliber team.

00:00:58.683 --> 00:01:00.518
- [Announcer]: Ten seconds to go and a foul.

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:03.271
Cage will go to the line.

00:01:03.271 --> 00:01:05.315
Oden picks up his fifth foul.

00:01:05.523 --> 00:01:07.776
The NCAA tournament, Xavier,

00:01:07.776 --> 00:01:09.903
I was sitting on the bench like, "I'm about to have 

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:12.197
a spring break for the first time in my life.

00:01:12.197 --> 00:01:14.115
- [Announcer]: Conley, five to go.

00:01:14.115 --> 00:01:16.534
Lewis has been awesome. Lets it go...

00:01:16.785 --> 00:01:18.244
brings it home!

00:01:19.329 --> 00:01:21.331
He ties it at 62!

00:01:21.331 --> 00:01:24.292
- And then the overtime came and Mike Conley,

00:01:24.292 --> 00:01:27.003
I think he got seven points to start the overtime.

00:01:27.003 --> 00:01:29.005
Me and him was watching the film after

00:01:29.005 --> 00:01:32.383
in the hotel, and just looking at him smile and

00:01:32.383 --> 00:01:36.721
actually seeing all that, that work and that emotion he put out there.

00:01:36.721 --> 00:01:39.641
- We were giddy kids at the time, just enjoying it.

00:01:39.641 --> 00:01:41.351
And being able to watch the film, it was just like,

00:01:41.351 --> 00:01:44.187
"Yeah, that really happened. Man, I can't believe that happpened."

00:01:44.187 --> 00:01:45.271
It felt like we couldn't lose after that.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:48.858
- We definitely knew how good Tennessee was.

00:01:48.858 --> 00:01:50.443
- [Announcer]: Rebound, Tennessee.

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:51.236
- Big rebound.

00:01:51.236 --> 00:01:54.614
- I mostly remember my blocked shot at the end of the game.

00:01:55.865 --> 00:01:58.785
Ron Lew, like, screamed in my face afterwards.

00:02:00.036 --> 00:02:03.039
When I blocked that shot, my chin had hit the ground,

00:02:03.039 --> 00:02:05.875
and when it had hit the ground, it, like, cracked so many of my teeth

00:02:05.875 --> 00:02:07.544
and exposed so many of my cavities.

00:02:07.919 --> 00:02:09.129
We won the game, but I was like,

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:11.923
yeah, I was at the dentist for the next five weeks.

00:02:13.716 --> 00:02:19.097
- [Announcer]: Ohio State wins it 92-76.

00:02:19.597 --> 00:02:21.432
- His presence offensively, defensively, 

00:02:21.432 --> 00:02:23.768
he changes the whole dynamic of a whole team.

00:02:23.768 --> 00:02:25.478
We were so used to having him there as an anchor.

00:02:26.563 --> 00:02:31.276
- [Announcer]: The Buckeyes buy a ticket to Monday night's finals.

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:36.322
Ohio State and Florida for the national championship.

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:38.491
- That national championship game, you know, 

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:40.785
we're all nervous sitting in the locker room,

00:02:40.785 --> 00:02:43.788
and we're like, "What's Coach Matta gonna say to get us riled up?"

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:46.583
And then he walks in, he turns off the light, and

00:02:46.583 --> 00:02:48.042
he puts on this clip from

00:02:48.042 --> 00:02:49.002
"Wedding Crashers."

00:02:49.377 --> 00:02:50.378
- Damn you.

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:53.214
I almost nunchucked you, you don't even realize!

00:02:53.631 --> 00:02:54.382
- Ouch.

00:02:54.382 --> 00:02:55.508
- "I almost nunchucked you!"

00:02:55.884 --> 00:02:58.219
That's what we watched before the national championship game.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:00.388
And then the game started, and I think 

00:03:00.388 --> 00:03:03.433
our sense of urgency kinda kicked in a little bit too late.

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:06.853
- We threw a lot of bodies at 'em.

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:09.689
The strength of our team was that we just could

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:10.899
keep throwing bigs at 'em,

00:03:11.983 --> 00:03:12.942
and good ones too.

00:03:13.568 --> 00:03:16.946
- Joakim Noah, Al Horford, those are the guys that

00:03:16.946 --> 00:03:18.698
I had to go up against.

00:03:19.115 --> 00:03:22.202
So yeah, I definitely got tired. Like, they definitely wore me out.

00:03:24.662 --> 00:03:28.166
That team was a great team. You know, two national championships.

00:03:28.166 --> 00:03:33.004
But you need to tell the Florida fans that doing the Gator Chomp

00:03:33.004 --> 00:03:34.797
to an 18-year-old kid after he just

00:03:34.797 --> 00:03:37.258
lost the national championship is—

00:03:37.926 --> 00:03:41.179
I almost cried walking off that court right there.

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:43.348
- You know what? I would've probably been crying too.

00:03:43.932 --> 00:03:45.058
I'm happy we won, though.

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:49.812
- I loved it here in Columbus, Ohio. But when the opportunity

00:03:49.812 --> 00:03:51.481
comes to be the No. 1 draft pick,

00:03:51.481 --> 00:03:53.066
I think you gotta take that.

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:58.363
- With the first pick in the 2007 NBA draft,

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:03.243
the Portland Trail Blazers select Greg Oden

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:05.286
from Ohio State University.

00:04:05.995 --> 00:04:07.705
- [Announcer]: Scola gives Brooks the pick.

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:09.165
Uh-oh.

00:04:09.165 --> 00:04:10.124
Oh, Greg.

00:04:10.124 --> 00:04:11.417
Greg went down and—

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:12.377
Oh, his knee is—

00:04:14.045 --> 00:04:15.964
Holy cow, Portland doesn't need this.

00:04:15.964 --> 00:04:18.549
- When I was an NBA player for those six years,

00:04:18.549 --> 00:04:22.220
I was rarely on the floor, just with all those injuries I've had,

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:24.055
I didn't feel like I did enough.

00:04:24.055 --> 00:04:25.598
I physically could not do it.

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:28.851
It was like if I gave one good day of that hard work,

00:04:29.477 --> 00:04:32.355
the next three days I spent rehabbing, just

00:04:32.355 --> 00:04:35.358
trying to get my knees to feel good for me to 

00:04:35.358 --> 00:04:37.694
sit down or walk down the stairs.

00:04:37.694 --> 00:04:39.404
It was so much pain I was going through

00:04:39.404 --> 00:04:43.616
just to try to get myself to the level I wanted to be at.

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:47.704
- I think bust is a tough term because his was

00:04:47.704 --> 00:04:50.623
injury-driven, not skill-driven.

00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:53.209
We all saw what he can do. His athleticism, 

00:04:53.209 --> 00:04:55.086
his ability, there's no bust about that.

00:04:55.253 --> 00:04:57.672
- People call whatever they want a bust.

00:04:58.006 --> 00:05:02.593
In the context, compared to some, I can see it that way too.

00:05:02.927 --> 00:05:05.305
And then some people get mad at me for saying that.

00:05:05.305 --> 00:05:07.265
It's like, "Don't talk that way about yourself,"

00:05:07.265 --> 00:05:08.224
and I'm like, "Oh, OK."

00:05:09.267 --> 00:05:10.601
But, you know, it's just a word.

00:05:10.601 --> 00:05:13.855
When I was deciding if I was going to be done playing basketball,

00:05:13.855 --> 00:05:16.816
it was definitely a mental switch I had to make.

00:05:16.816 --> 00:05:21.529
A lot of watching old YouTube clips and, you know, crying by myself.

00:05:21.529 --> 00:05:23.781
I picked up the phone and called Coach Matta.

00:05:23.781 --> 00:05:25.450
It was actually the greatest thing I did.

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:28.202
He was just like, "Come be around the program. Come be around

00:05:28.202 --> 00:05:31.080
the guys. Stay around basketball. Stay around, you know,

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:34.083
just basketball minds." You know, keeping that open

00:05:34.083 --> 00:05:37.253
to give me a reason to wake up and just go to the gym.

00:05:37.253 --> 00:05:38.671
You know, to see people.

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:41.424
- When big fella told me he was going back to school to

00:05:41.424 --> 00:05:43.301
be a coach, get his degree,

00:05:43.926 --> 00:05:45.386
I was happy. I was proud of him.

00:05:45.386 --> 00:05:49.557
- So, when I graduate, I want my spot to be right here.

00:05:49.557 --> 00:05:53.519
I'm gonna graduate and finish my undergrad in May.

00:05:53.519 --> 00:05:54.479
Don't second-guess.

00:05:56.064 --> 00:05:57.523
He ain't blocking you straight up.

00:05:57.523 --> 00:05:59.567
I want to go into coaching next.

00:05:59.776 --> 00:06:03.404
I really enjoy trying to figure out this new game of basketball.

00:06:03.404 --> 00:06:05.073
- He's got so much to teach, so much

00:06:05.073 --> 00:06:06.491
to, you know, give to these guys.

00:06:06.491 --> 00:06:08.618
I hope they enjoy having me here. 

00:06:08.618 --> 00:06:12.121
I hope I'm telling them things that's gonna impact their lives

00:06:12.121 --> 00:06:13.915
on and off the court.

00:06:13.915 --> 00:06:16.334
And I hope they enjoy it as much as I do.

